XpadUhid: poll rate 0, so the hidraw queue drains

The source loop reads one HID report per pass (read_timeout, 10 ms) and
then sleeps for the rest of the driver's poll rate. XpadUhid (Bluetooth
LE Xbox pads through BlueZ's uhid) had 500 ms: two reports a second, while
the pad sends one about every 30 ms. The reports queued in the hidraw
buffer (64 of them) and input came up to ~30 s late. Upstream commit
6d08364 ("Use blocking read mechanism only for hidraw source polling")
set every event-driven hidraw driver to 0 ms for this reason, but left
XpadUhid at 500 ms (still so on master, 2026-10). The 10 ms read timeout
paces the loop.

--- a/src/input/source/hidraw.rs
+++ b/src/input/source/hidraw.rs
@@ -515,7 +515,7 @@
             }
             DriverType::XpadUhid => {
                 let options = SourceDriverOptions {
-                    poll_rate: Duration::from_millis(500),
+                    poll_rate: Duration::from_millis(0),
                     buffer_size: 1024,
                 };
                 let device = XpadUhid::new(device_info.clone())?;
